octopkg-tui is a terminal user interface for pkg(8), the FreeBSD package
manager. It is the terminal counterpart of OctoPkg, with the same tabs and
shortcuts whenever the terminal allows, and it needs neither Qt nor X11, so
it also works over SSH.

Features:
- Installed and repository package views, with OctoPkg's states
  (installed, dependency, outdated, newer, locked, not installed)
- Details and file lists, search by name or description, a category
  filter, and sorting by any column
- Mark packages to install (+) or remove (-), preview the transaction
  (pkg install -n, pkg remove -n) and apply it
- Upgrade, database sync, cache cleaning, lock and unlock
- Optional boot environment (bectl) before each transaction
- The latest news of the system (FreeBSD, NomadBSD, HardenedBSD, GhostBSD,
  DragonFly BSD), fetched with fetch(1)
- Privileges through doas or sudo, only for the operations
- 15 color themes, Nerd Font, Unicode or ASCII icons, and English,
  Brazilian Portuguese and Spanish translations
